# XCU m4
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# m4 driven by input files; every expectation is built with printf or
# heredocs. Output of dumpdef, traceon and the -s directive text are
# unspecified and only minimally checked.

assertion  XCU.m4.001
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       A macro defined with define expands with $1, $2, $0 and $#
           replaced; without parentheses $# is 0 and arguments are null; the
           expansion is rescanned; names are the longest run of letters,
           digits and underscores not starting with a digit.
test       t/001-define-args.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.002
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Parenthesised commas do not split arguments, leading white space
           of an argument is dropped and trailing kept, omitted arguments
           are null, $* joins with commas, and $@ quotes each argument so it
           is not expanded again.
test       t/002-argument-collection.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.003
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Quoted text is not expanded and the outer quotes are removed;
           changequote sets and restores the quote strings; comment text is
           copied unscanned; changecom changes the comment start; dnl
           discards through the newline.
test       t/003-quotes-comments-dnl.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.004
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       ifelse chooses by string equality, handles the 4,5 and 6-or-more
           argument forms; incr, decr, len, index, substr, translit and
           shift give the specified strings.
test       t/004-conditionals-strings.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.005
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       pushdef saves a definition that popdef restores; popdef of the
           last definition undefines; undefine removes all definitions;
           ifdef tests definition; defn gives a definition that can define
           another macro.
test       t/005-definitions.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.006
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       eval evaluates the listed C operators with C precedence, accepts
           octal and hexadecimal constants, and takes a radix and a minimum
           digit count as second and third arguments.
test       t/006-eval.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.007
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Diverted text is held and written at the end in buffer order;
           divert(-1) discards; divnum gives the current stream; undivert
           writes a buffer at once and empties it; m4wrap text is processed
           at end of input in call order.
test       t/007-diversions.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.008
anchor     utilities/m4.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/m4.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       -D defines to the value or to null, -U undefines (including
           built-ins), their order matters, options may follow operands,
           files are processed in order with - meaning standard input, and
           -s produces #line directives.
test       t/008-options-operands.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.009
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       include gives the contents of a file; sinclude of a missing file
           is silently empty with status 0; include of a missing file writes
           a diagnostic and the final status is non-zero.
test       t/009-include.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.010
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/m4.html#STDERR
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       syscmd runs a command and sysval gives its exit value; m4exit
           sets the exit status and stops processing; errprint writes to
           standard error only.
test       t/010-system-macros.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.011
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       mkstemp gives the pathname of a file it created from the template
           argument.
test       t/011-mkstemp.sh

assertion  XCU.m4.012
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/m4.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      2024
says       m4exit with no argument or a zero argument, after an error has
           occurred, leaves the exit status non-zero.
test       t/012-m4exit-after-error.sh
